The requirements to run this software are as follows:

- Linux
- A working docker distribution with the ability to allow for network requests to containers.
- Bash and the ability to run bash scripts on the machine.
- a GNU xargs installation available on the PATH
- a jq (https://github.com/jqlang/jq) installation on the PATH, also available as a package for ubuntu/debian/fedora/suse/arch (https://jqlang.github.io/jq/download/)
- an installation of curl available on the PATH

NOTE: Check the parallelism configuration outlined in the readme before building the container and running the benchmark script.
The prototype was originally run on a strong machine with a very large amount of RAM and a high core count processor and hence toning down these settings
may be beneficial for stability/resource usage but may make running the benchmark much longer.

